for the last two decades some of the  biggest gaming news and reveals have  come during the electronic entertainment  expo or  e3 the yearly video game industry trade  show where the newest titles and  products are on full display many for  the first time  but even though the show has drawn tens  of thousands of people  to its convention centers every summer  the show itself has gone through  a whole lot of changes during this 27  year long run  well 26 if you exclude the cancel one  last year  so let's take a look back at the history  of e3 and maybe laugh at all the dorky  90s outfits strap yourself  in cause we're going to e3  here we are in 1985 the gaming industry  was attempting to recover from the  market crash two years prior and  ces the consumer electronics show was  the primary convention for hardware  makers to show off the newest consoles  and games  video games would continue to thrive  after the release of the nintendo  entertainment system but there still  wasn't a dedicated gaming convention  for all the newest releases for the next  10 years they had to share the spotlight  with the latest televisions cameras  and the batmobile and so that brings us  to 1995  right in the middle of the decade a 19  year old tiger woods was dominating the  amateur golf world  bill gates was busy launching the newest  version of windows with  jay leno for some reason but more  importantly  the interactive digital software  association now known as the  entertainment software association  or esa was quietly putting together the  biggest  game trade show in the world i'm kurt  lowder with mtv news connoisseurs of  video games computer effluvia and all  the latest in electronic gizmo mania  converged on los angeles last week  the annual electronic entertainment expo  better known as e3  okay 50 000 members of the press in its  first year is  hardly quiet in fact the gaming world  got an  earful of big console announcements from  the three biggest publishers at the time  sony sega and nintendo during e3 1995  sony revealed the original playstation's  release date and price  the sega saturn for some reason started  immediately shipping  to retailers and nintendo showcased the  virtual boy  ah well i i guess one out of three ain't  so bad  and that was in addition to all the  third-party developers who also showed  up 3do  capcom activision ea squaresoft all  attended but their presence was dwarfed  by none other  than acclaim who brought in over 15  different games to the show  e3's first year ended up being one of  the biggest conventions to date  and encouraged the organizers to  continue having the show  in los angeles every summer and they did  for the next two years at least while  sunny california might have been the  perfect spot for e3 due to some  unfortunate negotiation problems the  location was  actually moved to atlanta georgia for  1997 and 1998.  nevertheless e3 continued to grow in  size and upon returning to the la  convention center the attendance  remained at a steady  60 to 70 000 people strong that's quite  a lot of people  but there were quite a lot of games  there as well  e3 1999 featured sega's new dreamcast  console in full  force as well as some previews of sony's  new playstation  at e3 2000 we saw the first appearance  of computer software giant  microsoft who were preparing for the  release of their first video game  console the xbox you'll be able to get a  box just like this  with xbox in it e3 2001 was the final  appearance of sega as a console maker  after making the decision to focus on  software only  but we also got the first look at  nintendo's latest system  the gamecube as well as the first  trailer for super smash bros melee  which by the way is still one of the  biggest fighting games  today so the new big three sony nintendo  and now  microsoft kind of cruised along for a  few years it wasn't until e3  2006 that sony decided to make history  with one of the weirdest press  conferences  ever game is powered by namco it's ridge  racer  ridge racer remember that one  so here's this giant enemy crab was the  unintentional goofiness of sony's press  conference the tipping point  probably not but the giant enemy crab  sure didn't help anything  flip over this crab on its back  if he shows up and you attack its  weak point for massive damage the  following year  citing budget issues among some  publishers then esa  president doug lowenstein announced that  e3 would now be a smaller  more intimate event with an invite-only  list of about 10  000 people this shift essentially shut  out many bloggers and non-industry  professionals that had attended the show  in previous years  but with the new look also came a new  name e3  media and business summit also e3 that  year wasn't held at the typical los  angeles convention center  nor was it held in any sort of central  location at all  it was actually spread across different  venues and locations in santa monica  and if you weren't part of the industry  at the time you probably wouldn't have  even realized it was happening gone were  the gaudy displays and  sensory overload of previous years and  in their place were hotel  ballrooms and jamie kennedy from  neversoft which wasn't that the first  name for viagra i don't despite the  changes being made to try and improve  the show  it was still an exceedingly tough time  for e3 with sims creator  will wright saying that the conference  quote almost feels  like a zombie at this point but hey at  least we got a few memes  out of the deal my body my body is ready  thankfully for will wright and many  other people who once enjoyed attending  e3  the show is actually opened back up to a  larger audience in 2009 with over 40  000 people coming back to check out the  latest games such as metal gear rising  final fantasy 14  and super mario galaxy 2. the slight  misstep didn't seem to matter all that  much as e3 continued to be the biggest  name in gaming trade shows though there  has been  no shortage of awkward press conferences  in the years since  there is ubisoft's in 2015. do you have  a meme one up you want a pitch  oh we had mr caffeine in 2011. everyone  do it with me  i said and of course konami's in  2010. this is not the original hack and  slash anymore  this is an extreme  extreme heck of trash title  but as we all know e3 isn't about memes  mostly with the 27 year history behind  it there's also been changes in the way  publishers approach the show companies  like ubisoft have continuously attempted  to bring more personality and humor to  their press conferences though their  success rate is up for  debate and nintendo stopped doing live  press conferences entirely in 2013  to focus on their pre-recorded showcases  dubbed nintendo  direct and in 2017 e3 itself changed  everything by opening its doors to the  public for the very first time  meaning that anyone was able to buy  tickets and attend the show  gone are the days where the latest  gaming announcements and showcases are  coveted  for industry-centric folk the gates had  been opened to the public  it was an enormous success and a  claustrophobic one  2017 saw 68 000 attendees flocking to e3  resulting in an overcrowded convention  center with enthusiastic game players  shoulder the shoulder and butts to butts  thankfully the tradition of e3's  inclusivity to the public  continued in 2018 with the caveat  of giving industry only access for the  first few hours before  the public the result drew in 69 000  attendees making it the largest since  2005.  nice and its attendance wasn't the only  big deal  microsoft took the stage to announce the  acquisition of ninja theory undead  labs playground games and compulsion  games  bethesda kicked off with a full-blown  rock concert thanks to andrew wk  followed with todd howard staring  longingly at a map  that's right  so cool and while bethesda had the party  god  sony had flute guy in fact sony did a  lot of things different that year  instead of the usual series of teasers  and announcements  sony went all in on deep dive  presentations for the last of us part 2  goes to sushima and spider-man also  as it would turn out it would be sony's  last e3 spectacle  to this day sony opted not to  participate in 2019's e3  the first time since the expo's  inception 25 years prior  in an interview sony ceo sean laden said  that the trade show  was no longer helpful due in part to the  rapid news flow of the internet and a  shift for sony to focus on fewer  but more quality games but while sony  wasn't there  thankfully keanu reeves was  you're breathtaking which brings us to  2020 the year the world came to a halt  and pivoted in the face of the coven 19  pandemic  as a result e3 was cancelled only a  month  prior still the spirit of gaming  excitement and announcements lived on  with companies turning to their own  style of nintendo-like directs  and while we still paddle through the  ripples of the pandemic e3  is returning this year with an all  digital event  so even through its ups and downs and  even a cancellation under its belt  e3 has been and continues to be a place  for media publishers  and now the gaming public to gather and  celebrate video games and all of their  wonderful  and sometimes weird glory  so here's to more e3 to more  jaw-dropping reveals  more awkward moments and goofy press  conferences  and most importantly more games not only  new games forever  but new gamers forever  thank you very much  you

